  "body": "Session closeout for the 2026-05-25 mid-afternoon → 2026-05-26 mid-afternoon arc. First session occupying the catdef-strategist seat under the ratified identity (CA-009). **What was drafted (with paths):** (1) decisions/CA-008.md — Track decomposition + Anthropic-arc strategic context + catdef.org/mcp introduction; (2) decisions/CA-009.md — strategist + maintainer bot identity ratification + CA-NNN namespace unification (sunset CDF-NNNN); (3) decisions/CA-010.md — designated reference user pattern formalized; Thingalog designated as first reference user; (4) decisions/CA-013.md — three housekeeping calls (sunset legacy /feedback createGitHubIssue; add GitHub Actions deploy workflow; ratify canonical-implementor bot identity); (5) six outbound memos: 2026-05-25-1700 → thingalog-strategist (plugin disposition); 2026-05-25-1900 → canonical-implementor (plugin packaging brief with render-engine addition filed via a small follow-on commit per Director directive); 2026-05-25-2100 → thingalog-strategist (gap dispositions first read, strict value-#4 interpretation); 2026-05-25-2200 → thingalog-strategist (revised dispositions per CA-010, supersedes 2100 in part); 2026-05-26-1500 → canonical-implementor (v0.1.1 bundle handoff); (6) three MCP feedback submissions filed dogfood-style via catdef_report_feedback (CA-011, CA-012, CA-014) — all triaged via catdef_set_feedback_status; (7) README.md updates for post-v1.4 state (165 tests, MCP surface section, decisions/ row added, Feedback section split into AI-peer-MCP and human-email channels). **What was decided:** strategist-level dispositions across 4 CA-NNN decisions captured above; v1.5 work pickup list explicitly re-ordered in the 2026-05-25-2200 body_ref (Primary-index Phase 2 LEAD; value-shape bundle of CA-007 + OQ8 follow-on + item-level polymorphism + rich-Value internal structure as coordinated design; MCP-conformance + theme-spec restructure as parallel tracks; audio attachment deferred pending PXMemories ship on revised empirical-surface grounds). **What's in flight (started but didn't land):** (a) canonical-implementor's v0.1.1 bundle — CA-011 fix landed during this session (verified via post-fix catdef_list_decisions call returning 9 decisions cleanly); CA-012 + CA-013 Calls 1 + 2 still queued for that seat's continued work; (b) catdef-maintainer governance-text updates per CA-013 Call 3 (canonical-implementor bot identity acknowledgment in org artifact + CLAUDE.md known-work-items) — flagged as no urgency in v0.1.1 handoff; (c) Plugin marketplace submission — PO web-form action; outside strategist seat. **What's open (items surfaced but not addressed):** (a) CA-014 (schema-vocabulary translation: input enum vocabulary differs from queue-display vocabulary) — triaged; queued for v0.1.2 or v0.2 cycle; preferred fix is unifying input + storage schemas; (b) v1.5 cycle remains queued — Director triggers when ready; Primary-index Phase 2 leads; (c) Thingalog standard MCP key — optional; mint when thingalog-strategist files a request memo OR pre-mint per Director's preference. **Notable session-arc observations (worth carrying forward in seat history):** (1) The 21:00 first-read on gap dispositions applied value #4 cross-implementer-demand strictly; PO pushback ('we know that a use case is coming, and we really want Thingalog to be a reference user of catdef') led to CA-010 reference-user pattern formalization; the 22:00 revision supersedes-in-part. Both memos preserved as institutional record. Generalizable lesson: when a value's strict reading is tighter than the spec's own practice (canonical reference file already drives single-implementer promotion), formalizing the pattern via CA-NNN beats either holding the strict line or ad-hoc loosening it. (2) catdef.org/mcp v0.1 was stood up by canonical-implementor during this session arc; this seat performed the first dogfood test which surfaced CA-011 + CA-012 + CA-014. Strong empirical validation of CA-008 Track D: the feedback channel handled its first real catdef-side feedback during the same session it was instantiated. Eating own dogfood worked. (3) The CA-NNN collision risk PO accepted (option c) during the v0.1.1 fix window did NOT materialize. CA-014 was allocated cleanly post-CA-011-fix (counter resynced past decisions/CA-013.md); the option-c risk acceptance turned out to be the right call. (4) Strategist decisions on main went via direct commit (rule bypass under Director auth); maintainer governance bundle went via admin-merged PR (#40). Two workflow patterns now established and both ratified by usage. Future strategist sessions inherit the choice: direct-commit for small/routine decisions; PR-shape for larger or coordinated work. **What future incumbents of this seat should know on next onboarding:** (i) The reference-user pattern (CA-010) is now established — gap-proposals from Thingalog qualify for v1.5 promotion without external-implementer demand demonstration. Criteria for additional designations codified in CA-010 §Criteria for future designations. (ii) The catdef.org/mcp queue is the operational workplace; catdef_list_feedback is the seat's primary visibility into the inbound; check it early in onboarding. (iii) The strategist's elevated MCP key is held by PO (cdfk_dir_<random>; D1 holds hash only); request via memo or in-chat when staffing. (iv) v1.5 trigger is the Director's call; this seat does not unilaterally launch the cycle; when triggered, Primary-index Phase 2 (Gap 3 from 2026-05-25-2000) leads. (v) The supersedes-in-part pattern (2100 → 2200 here) is fine and preserves institutional record; don't overwrite or delete superseded memos. (vi) The MCP server's input + storage vocabulary mismatch (CA-014) is real but minor; AI peers may see different category/severity values in queue display vs what they submitted until fix lands. (vii) When the v0.1.1 bundle (CA-012 + CA-013 Calls 1 + 2) ships, expect a status memo back from canonical-implementor; standard milestone-reporting pattern.",
